[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "2609.09830 does not quote an LZ-excluded delta_m0 range. Its five benchmarks (|mu| = 0.61-1.40 TeV; |M1|, M2 about 5.8-42 TeV; tan beta 10.9-26.5) ha
[finding] f-002 2609.09830 does not quote an LZ-excluded delta_m0 range. Its five benchmarks (|mu| = 0.61-1.40 TeV; |M1|, M2 about 5.8-42 TeV; tan beta 10.9-26.5) have one-loop
**Finding:** 2609.09830 does not quote an LZ-excluded delta_m0 range. Its five benchmarks (|mu| = 0.61-1.40 TeV; |M1|, M2 about 5.8-42 TeV; tan beta 10.9-26.5) have one-loop on-shell splittings delta = 8.9-36.4 keV. Each predicts at most about 1.03 combined NLO events in LZ, and probing them needs 9.4-65.5 tonne-years. All are consistent with the LZ bound. Inelastic events at NLO range from 0.00022 (BP1) to 0.18 (BP4). NLO vertex corrections can exceed 100 percent, and in BP2 the inelastic cross section is about twice the LO elastic one. Splittings of O(10) keV come from partial cancellation of the M_Z^2/M1 and M_Z^2/M2 terms when M1 and M2 have opposite signs.
[tool] tc-261016_1-w1-d-03-51 -> ok: Recorded finding f-002.
[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "2606.31013: the SI coupling comes from Higgs exchange, f_q ~ -(g^2/8M_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 theta_W/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta), so it is su
[finding] f-003 2606.31013: the SI coupling comes from Higgs exchange, f_q ~ -(g^2/8M_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 theta_W/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta), so it is suppressed at
**Finding:** 2606.31013: the SI coupling comes from Higgs exchange, f_q ~ -(g^2/8M_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 theta_W/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta), so it is suppressed at large gaugino mass and at small tan beta with mu<0. The scan covers 150<|mu|<1000 GeV, 1.6<tan beta<50, 0.5<M1<10 TeV with M2=2M1. Rates are rescaled by Omega_H h^2/0.12 (Eq. 38, computed with micrOMEGAs 6.3.0). Direct detection is sensitive mainly where higgsino-gaugino mixing produces sizable charged-neutral splittings, and reaches the thermal mass of about 1 TeV. The radiative charged-neutral splitting tends to about 356 MeV for M >> M_Z (Eq. 13).
