[tool] d-02 post_finding {"claim": "Hisano et al. (1104.0228) find the leading-order electroweak-loop SI cross section of pure EW-multiplet DM (including the higgsino, n=2, Y=1/2, evalu
[finding] f-004 Hisano et al. (1104.0228) find the leading-order electroweak-loop SI cross section of pure EW-multiplet DM (including the higgsino, n=2, Y=1/2, evaluated at M=1
**Finding:** Hisano et al. (1104.0228) find the leading-order electroweak-loop SI cross section of pure EW-multiplet DM (including the higgsino, n=2, Y=1/2, evaluated at M=1 TeV) to be O(1e-46 to 1e-48) cm^2, suppressed by an accidental cancellation: twist-2 contributions are positive while Higgs-exchange, gluon and scalar contributions are negative, and they are of similar size. The cross section is nearly independent of mass above about 1 TeV.
[tool] tc-261016_1-w1-d-02-56 -> ok: Recorded finding f-004.
[tool] d-02 post_finding {"claim": "LZ 2024 (2410.17036, 4.2 tonne-years): the strongest SI exclusion is 2.2e-48 cm^2 (90% CL) and the best median sensitivity is 5.1e-48 cm^2, both at 4
[finding] f-005 LZ 2024 (2410.17036, 4.2 tonne-years): the strongest SI exclusion is 2.2e-48 cm^2 (90% CL) and the best median sensitivity is 5.1e-48 cm^2, both at 40 GeV/c^2. 
**Finding:** LZ 2024 (2410.17036, 4.2 tonne-years): the strongest SI exclusion is 2.2e-48 cm^2 (90% CL) and the best median sensitivity is 5.1e-48 cm^2, both at 40 GeV/c^2. The abstract quotes no value at 1 TeV.
