[tool] d-01 post_finding {"claim": "Beneke, Hellmann and Ruiz-Femenia (arXiv:1411.6930, Sec. 3) report Omega h^2 = 0.127 (perturbative) and 0.126 (Sommerfeld, with off-diagonal rates) f
[finding] f-007 Beneke, Hellmann and Ruiz-Femenia (arXiv:1411.6930, Sec. 3) report Omega h^2 = 0.127 (perturbative) and 0.126 (Sommerfeld, with off-diagonal rates) for a pure-h
**Finding:** Beneke, Hellmann and Ruiz-Femenia (arXiv:1411.6930, Sec. 3) report Omega h^2 = 0.127 (perturbative) and 0.126 (Sommerfeld, with off-diagonal rates) for a pure-higgsino model compared against the higgsino-like pMSSM point 1627006 at m_chi = 1172.31 GeV. The net Sommerfeld correction for pure higgsinos is almost zero (below 1 percent) because enhancement in the neutral channels cancels suppression in the chi0 chi+- channels. For the pMSSM higgsino-like point (higgsino fraction 0.98, dm+ = 1.8 GeV, dm0 = 9.5 GeV) they find Omega h^2 = 0.108 (perturbative) and 0.100 (Sommerfeld), an 8 percent reduction. The quoted Sommerfeld accuracy is about 5 percent at best.
