[finding] f-008 Chen and Hill (1912.07795) include the O(mW/M) power corrections, perturbative QCD to NNNLO and ChEFT nuclear effects. They find that the pure-higgsino SI cross
**Finding:** Chen and Hill (1912.07795) include the O(mW/M) power corrections, perturbative QCD to NNNLO and ChEFT nuclear effects. They find that the pure-higgsino SI cross section has an upper limit below 1e-48 cm^2 in the TeV mass range, below the estimated xenon neutrino floor. This is about 2 orders of magnitude below the LZ 2024 minimum limit of 2.2e-48 cm^2 at 40 GeV. Assuming linear mass scaling of the LZ limit above about 100 GeV (my estimate, not read from the paper), the LZ limit at 1.1 TeV is about 2.2e-48 x (1100/40), roughly 6e-47 cm^2, so the pure higgsino lies at least about 1.8 orders of magnitude below it.
