[tool] d-01 post_finding {"claim": "Hisano et al. (hep-ph/0610249) expect the Sommerfeld effect on the higgsino-like relic abundance to be roughly 10 percent, compared with a 50 percent
[finding] f-009 Hisano et al. (hep-ph/0610249) expect the Sommerfeld effect on the higgsino-like relic abundance to be roughly 10 percent, compared with a 50 percent reduction 
**Finding (preliminary):** Hisano et al. (hep-ph/0610249) expect the Sommerfeld effect on the higgsino-like relic abundance to be roughly 10 percent, compared with a 50 percent reduction for the wino. 1411.6930 later found the net pure-higgsino effect is below 1 percent (Omega h^2 = 0.127 perturbative, 0.126 Sommerfeld). Rescaling that single point (taken as m = 1172.31 GeV) with Omega h^2 proportional to m^2 gives the Planck value 0.120 at m of about 1.14 TeV (Sommerfeld: 1144 GeV; perturbative: 1139 GeV). The rescaled values are 0.074, 0.092, 0.111, 0.132 and 0.155 at m = 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 1.2 and 1.3 TeV. These are m^2 rescalings of one published point, not published values.
[tool] tc-261016_1-w1-d-01-69 -> ok: Recorded finding f-009.
