[tool] d-06 post_finding {"claim": "The full text of 2606.31013 supports the f-003 numbers. Eq. 13 reads Delta m+|rad ~ (1/2) alpha2 MZ sin^2 thetaW (1 - 3MZ/(2 pi M_chi+)), with the st
[finding] f-015 The full text of 2606.31013 supports the f-003 numbers. Eq. 13 reads Delta m+|rad ~ (1/2) alpha2 MZ sin^2 thetaW (1 - 3MZ/(2 pi M_chi+)), with the statement 'Fo
**Finding:** The full text of 2606.31013 supports the f-003 numbers. Eq. 13 reads Delta m+|rad ~ (1/2) alpha2 MZ sin^2 thetaW (1 - 3MZ/(2 pi M_chi+)), with the statement 'For M_chi+ >> MZ, this mass splitting asymptotically approaches Delta m+|rad ~ 356 MeV'. Eq. 33 reads f_q ~ -(g^2/8M_h^2)[1/(M2-|mu|) + tan^2 thetaW/(M1-|mu|)](1 + sgn(mu) sin 2beta) and is valid for MZ << M1,2-|mu|; the exact form is Eq. 32. The paper says the coupling is suppressed at large gaugino mass and 'for small tan beta and negative mu, due to an accidental cancellation'. Eq. 38 is sigma_SI/SD,eff = (Omega_H h^2/0.12) sigma_SI/SD, computed with micrOMEGAs v6.3.0. The scan (Eq. 37) covers 150 GeV<|mu|<1000 GeV, 1.6<tan beta<50 and 0.5 TeV<M1<10 TeV, with M2=2M1 and M1>|mu|. Note: the f-003 label 'Eq. 13' is correct; the f_q formula is Eq. 33, not unnumbered.
