[tool] d-06 post_finding {"claim": "The full text of 2609.09830 supports the f-002 numbers. Table III gives one-loop on-shell delta = 36.37, 8.90, 16.39, 10.81 and 10.59 keV for BP1-BP5
[finding] f-016 The full text of 2609.09830 supports the f-002 numbers. Table III gives one-loop on-shell delta = 36.37, 8.90, 16.39, 10.81 and 10.59 keV for BP1-BP5, with mu =
**Finding:** The full text of 2609.09830 supports the f-002 numbers. Table III gives one-loop on-shell delta = 36.37, 8.90, 16.39, 10.81 and 10.59 keV for BP1-BP5, with mu = -739.63, -606.64, -814.26, 1282.11 and 1400.0 GeV, M1 = -7830, -6292, -5838, 11354 and 12875 GeV, M2 = 17055, 42000, 30925, 12627 and 12050 GeV, and tan beta = 10.88-26.46. Table VII, NLO rows for BP1-BP5: elastic events 1.0280, 0.07729, 0.1176, 0.4127, 0.5074; inelastic events 0.00022, 0.07039, 0.0518, 0.1806, 0.1661; combined 1.02822, 0.14768, 0.1694, 0.5933, 0.6735; required exposure 9.41, 65.50, 57.10, 16.30, 14.36 t-y (LZ exposure 4.2 t-y; null result taken as N_E < ln 10, about 2.3). Table VI for BP2 gives sigma_inel NLO = 0.507e-12 pb against sigma_el LO = 0.284e-12 pb (ratio 1.785). The paper describes this as 'approximately a factor of two larger than the elastic LO one'. The text says all BPs are consistent with LZ. Note: the BP1 scan sign pattern has M1<0 and M2>0 for mu=±0.5 or ±1 TeV, with -21 TeV <= M1 <= -1 TeV and 1 TeV <= M2 <= 21 TeV (Eq. 25), yet BP4 and BP5 have M1 and M2 both positive.
[tool] tc-261016_1-w2-d-06-101 -> ok: Recorded finding f-016.
[tool] d-06 post_finding {"claim": "2609.09830 does not write out the tree-level delta_m0 formula. It says only: 'as can be seen, for example, from Eq. (9) of Ref. [28], the corrections
[finding] f-017 2609.09830 does not write out the tree-level delta_m0 formula. It says only: 'as can be seen, for example, from Eq. (9) of Ref. [28], the corrections proportion
**Finding:** 2609.09830 does not write out the tree-level delta_m0 formula. It says only: 'as can be seen, for example, from Eq. (9) of Ref. [28], the corrections proportional to M_Z^2/M1 and M_Z^2/M2 depend on the relative signs of M1 and M2. In the parameter regions relevant for our analysis, these contributions can have opposite signs and partially cancel.' 2606.31013 also says only that the splittings are 'suppressed by M_Z^2/M_1,2'. The explicit form delta_m0 ~ m_Z^2 s_W^2/M1 + m_Z^2 c_W^2/M2 therefore remains unsourced (q-05 stays open), and so does the estimate that same-sign M2=2M1 needs M1 of about 1.4e7 GeV. Counter-evidence to the 'tuned corners only' conclusion: BP4 and BP5 reach delta of about 10.6-10.8 keV with M1 and M2 both positive (about 11-13 TeV) and mu > 0. The O(10) keV splittings there come from on-shell one-loop corrections combined with relative signs between mu and the gauginos, not only from opposite-sign M1 and M2.
[tool] tc-261016_1-w2-d-06-102 -> ok: Recorded finding f-017.
